{"orgCode":"2320","name":"Department of Real Estate","agencyCode":"1000","agencyName":"Business and Consumer Services","description":"The mission of the Department of Real Estate is to safeguard and promote the public interests in real estate matters through licensure, regulation, education, and enforcement.","website":"https://www.dre.ca.gov","totals":{"amounts":{"py":60476,"cy":68457,"by":67620},"positions":{"py":329.9,"cy":374.7,"by":372.7},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":99,"cy":435,"by":435}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/1000/2320","kind":"department","name":"Department of Real Estate","code":"2320","amounts":{"py":60476,"cy":68457,"by":67620},"positions":{"py":329.9,"cy":374.7,"by":372.7},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":60476,"cy":68457,"by":67620}},"children":[{"id":"exp/1000/2320/1700","kind":"program","name":"Department of Real Estate","code":"1700","amounts":{"py":60476,"cy":68457,"by":67620},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":60476,"cy":68457,"by":67620}},"positions":{"py":329.9,"cy":374.7,"by":372.7},"description":"1700 - DEPARTMENT OF REAL ESTATE\n\nThe Department of Real Estate ensures that individuals who wish to engage in real estate business and act in the capacity of, or advertise as, a real estate broker or salesperson within California meet specified qualifications, including minimum education standards and requirements. The Department investigates the actions of any person acting in the capacity of a real estate licensee, performs financial compliance audits of licensees and subdividers, administratively prosecutes violations of the Real Estate Law and Subdivided Lands Law, and provides victims of real estate fraud with financial recovery per limitations set by statute. The Department protects the public against fraud and misrepresentation in the sale or lease of subdivided land through the issuance of public reports that disclose vital information to prospective purchasers of subdivision interests.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py"